	"changelog": "1.1.5: the licence now travels inside the package. COPYING.txt (GNU GPL v2) and LICENSE-PSL.txt (MPL 2.0, for the bundled Public Suffix List) are at the root of the .nvda-addon archive, beside manifest.ini. Add-on behaviour is unchanged. 1.1.4: the main shortcut is now NVDA+Control+Shift+L, because NVDA 2026.3 uses NVDA+Alt+L to increase the braille automatic scroll rate. NVDA+Alt+Shift+L still speaks the answer without a window. 1.1.3: copied files and images are recognised as such instead of being reported as a busy clipboard. Links, ordinary text, files and other clipboard formats are told apart before anything is sent. 1.1.2: text that is not a link is recognised and reported instead of being sent to Gemini. File names and dotted words are no longer mistaken for web addresses. 1.1.1: the Test the key button now opens a dialog with the result and a Close button, and the explanation window has a Close button and closes with Escape. 1.1.0: the explanation comes from Google Gemini and is shown in a read-only text window. You add your own free Gemini API key once. Checks use one short request per address, remember recent answers, and never open the link.",
